# Web Development - Modern Theme & Component Patterns

## MERN Stack (Full-Stack)

When the prompt mentions **MERN**, **MongoDB**, **Express**, **Node.js** (backend), or **full-stack JavaScript**:
- Use rule: `.cursor/rules/mern-stack.mdc`
- File structure: `docs/mern-stack/file-structure.md`
- Setup commands: `docs/mern-stack/setup-commands.md`
- Official docs: `docs/mern-stack/official-docs.md`
- Follow official Node, Express, MongoDB, React documentation conventions

## Full-stack website automation

The Web Development AI assistant generates a runnable site from `src/lib/websiteGenerator.ts` when a learner asks to build a website. It writes:

- `src/index.html`, `src/style.css`, `src/app.js` — browser client, previewed in the editor
- `src/server.js` — Express API (`GET /api/health`, `GET /api/items`, `POST /api/items`, `POST /api/contact`)
- `package.json`, `README.md`

`app.js` must stay browser-only and fall back when `/api/items` is unavailable. Do not inject `server.js` into the preview. Small UI requests still use one vanilla HTML file.

## Theme & Style

- **Design system**: Radix UI + shadcn/ui (radix-nova style)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with CSS variables (--primary, --foreground, --muted, --border, --card)
- **Aesthetic**: Modern, clean, accessible. Use semantic colors (text-foreground, text-muted-foreground, bg-card, border-border)
- **Animations**: Use tailwindcss-animate (accordion-up, accordion-down, etc.)

## Component Mapping

When the prompt mentions these concepts, use the corresponding pattern:

| Prompt keywords | Use component | Reference |
|-----------------|---------------|-----------|
| accordion, FAQ, expandable, collapsible sections, reveal content | Accordion | See accordion reference below |
| tabs, tabbed interface, switch views, segmented content | Tabs | See tabs reference below |
| alert, callout, notice, banner, info box, warning | Alert | docs/component-reference/alert.md |
| confirm dialog, confirmation modal, delete confirmation | AlertDialog | docs/component-reference/alert-dialog.md |
| cards, card layout | Card | @/components/ui/card |
| dialog, modal | Dialog | @/components/ui/dialog |
| dropdown, menu | DropdownMenu | @/components/ui/dropdown-menu |

## Accordion Reference (FAQ / Expandable Sections)

**Import:**
```tsx
import {
  Accordion,
  AccordionContent,
  AccordionItem,
  AccordionTrigger,
} from "@/components/ui/accordion"
```

**Basic usage (single item open):**
```tsx
<Accordion type="single" collapsible defaultValue="item-1">
  <AccordionItem value="item-1">
    <AccordionTrigger>Is it accessible?</AccordionTrigger>
    <AccordionContent>
      Yes. It adheres to the WAI-ARIA design pattern.
    </AccordionContent>
  </AccordionItem>
</Accordion>
```

**FAQ-style with bordered cards:**
```tsx
<Accordion type="single" collapsible className="space-y-3">
  {items.map((item, i) => (
    <AccordionItem
      key={i}
      value={`item-${i}`}
      className="rounded-lg border border-border bg-card px-6 transition-colors hover:border-primary/30"
    >
      <AccordionTrigger className="text-left text-sm font-semibold text-foreground hover:no-underline">
        {item.question}
      </AccordionTrigger>
      <AccordionContent className="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        {item.answer}
      </AccordionContent>
    </AccordionItem>
  ))}
</Accordion>
```

**Multiple items open:** Use `type="multiple"` on Accordion.

**Install:** `npx shadcn@latest add accordion` (or component already at `src/components/ui/accordion.tsx`)

## Tabs Reference (Tabbed Interface / Switch Views)

**Import:**
```tsx
import { Tabs, TabsList, TabsTrigger, TabsContent } from "@/components/ui/tabs"
```

**Basic usage:**
```tsx
<Tabs defaultValue="tab1">
  <TabsList>
    <TabsTrigger value="tab1">Tab 1</TabsTrigger>
    <TabsTrigger value="tab2">Tab 2</TabsTrigger>
  </TabsList>
  <TabsContent value="tab1">Content 1</TabsContent>
  <TabsContent value="tab2">Content 2</TabsContent>
</Tabs>
```

**Controlled with icons:**
```tsx
const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState("forum");
<Tabs value={activeTab} onValueChange={setActiveTab}>
  <TabsList>
    <TabsTrigger value="forum" className="gap-1.5"><PenSquare className="h-4 w-4" /> Forum</TabsTrigger>
    <TabsTrigger value="chat" className="gap-1.5"><MessageCircle className="h-4 w-4" /> Chat</TabsTrigger>
  </TabsList>
  <TabsContent value="forum">{/* ... */}</TabsContent>
  <TabsContent value="chat">{/* ... */}</TabsContent>
</Tabs>
```

**Full reference:** docs/component-reference/tabs.md

## JSX/React Preview & Vite

- **In-editor preview**: Uses Babel standalone + React 18 in-browser. Supports JSX, useState, useEffect, lucide-react icons (ShoppingBag, ShoppingCart, Plus, Minus, etc.). Unknown lucide icons render as placeholders.
- **lucide-react**: Use `import { IconName } from 'lucide-react'` — in-editor preview shims common icons. For full icon set, run locally with Vite.
- **Run locally with Vite** (for full npm packages): `npm create vite@latest my-app -- --template react && cd my-app && npm install lucide-react && npm run dev`

## Rule

When implementing web UI from a prompt:
1. Match prompt intent to the component mapping above
2. Use the exact import paths and patterns from this rule or docs/component-reference/
3. Preserve semantic styling (foreground, muted-foreground, card, border-border)
4. For Accordion: animations already in AccordionContent
5. For Tabs: use TabsList/TabsTrigger/TabsContent; add icons with `className="gap-1.5"` on TabsTrigger
6. For lucide-react: prefer icons in the shim (ShoppingBag, ShoppingCart, Plus, Minus, X, Heart, Star, etc.) so in-editor preview works
